### Compound-Assignment Audit (§2 & §2e)

Three compound-assignment sites were identified in [`Lasers.java`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/decompilation/java-src/Lasers.java), all inside `dt()` when `l1 != 0`:

#### Site 1 — `dt()` (Java line 91)
```java
ai[n4] += (int)(i - this.m.x + (Math.random() * 50.0 - 25.0));
```
- **Bytecode offsets & opcodes:**
  ```
  70: aload_2
  71: iload 16
  73: dup2
  74: iaload
  75: i2d                          // <-- Accumulator ai[l2] widened to double
  76: iload 5
  78: aload_0
  79: getfield #1 (m:LMedium;)
  82: getfield #9 (Medium.x:I)
  85: isub
  86: i2d                          // <-- (i - m.x) widened to double
  87: invokestatic #12 (Math.random:()D)
  90: ldc2_w 50.0d
  93: dmul
  94: ldc2_w 25.0d
  97: dsub
  98: dadd
  99: dadd
 100: d2i                          // <-- ONE truncation at the end
 101: iastore
  ```
- **Classification:** **Case A** (implicit narrowing cast inserted by `javac`; accumulator widened to double before addition, single `d2i` truncation at the end).
- **Correct JS:**
  ```js
  ai[n4] = trunc(ai[n4] + (i - this.m.x + (random() * 50.0 - 25.0)));
  ```
- **Mutation & Discriminating Test (§2e):**
  - Input separating Case A from Case B: `accumulator = 10`, `rhs = -0.4`.
  - Case A computes `trunc(10 + (-0.4)) = trunc(9.6) = 9`.
  - Case B computes `10 + trunc(-0.4) = 10 + 0 = 10`.
  - When mutated to Case B, the discriminator test fails (RED). Reverted to Case A (GREEN).

#### Site 2 — `dt()` (Java line 93)
```java
ai1[n5] += (int)(j - this.m.y + (Math.random() * 50.0 - 25.0));
```
- **Bytecode offsets & opcodes:**
  ```
  102: aload_3
  103: iload 16
  105: dup2
  106: iaload
  107: i2d                         // <-- Accumulator ai1[l2] widened to double
  ...
  130: dadd
  131: dadd
  132: d2i                         // <-- ONE truncation at the end
  133: iastore
  ```
- **Classification:** **Case A**.
- **Correct JS:**
  ```js
  ai1[n5] = trunc(ai1[n5] + (j - this.m.y + (random() * 50.0 - 25.0)));
  ```
- **Mutation result:** Confirmed separate from Case B; verified via discriminator test.

