### Preserved Bugs & Quirk Verbatim

- `d()` laser type 6 vs type 11 inner geometry: Laser geometry builds scratch arrays using integer truncation of `random()` floating expressions and stores to `ai`, `ai2`, `ai3` without out-of-bounds guards (relying on 3-vertex vs 4-vertex `dt()` calls).
- `dt()` color selection when `l1 != 0`: `i2 = 255; j2 = (l1 == 1 ? 235 : 220); k2 = (l1 == 1 ? 120 : 111);` overrides incoming `(i2, j2, k2)` parameters only if visible on screen (`flag == true`).
- `gsmoke()` and `hsmoke()` clamp `j1 > 3` to `j1 = 3` after constructing vertex arrays with the original `j1` value.

---

### Places Unsure What Java Does
None — All bytecode offsets and opcodes for arithmetic, conversions (`i2d`, `d2i`, `i2f`, `f2i`), array mutations, and polygon drawing were verified against the disassembled `Lasers.class`.

